  "major": "LVN-to-RN Career Ladder",
  "notes": "Transcribed from the official Mendocino College 2026 LVN-to-RN Program Brochure 'RN COURSES UNITS' table (three-term sequence: one short-term transition term + two full-time RN semesters). Modeled as accelerated per build.py convention (LPN-to-RN bridge; the 18-month program represents the 3rd and 4th semesters of the RN curriculum with advanced placement). Semester sums: 2 + 13 + 13 = 28. The brochure's printed total ('26') is a typo excluding the transition-term courses; the line items sum to 28, and the 2026-2027 catalog ('Total Major Units 28') and the official LVN-to-RN Certificate of Achievement document (LVN_CERT_25.pdf, 'Total units required for Certificate 28') both confirm 28. Course titles/units cross-verified against LVN_CERT_25.pdf. Prerequisites (per brochure, must be completed before entry with C or better): BIO 230 Human Anatomy, BIO 231 Human Physiology, BIO 239 (catalog: BIO 259) Microbiology (each 4+ semester units with lab, recency applies); ENGL C1000 English Composition; COMM C1000 or COMM 210; one of PSYC C1000, PSYC 210, CDV 200; one of SOC 200, SOC 201, ANT 201, ETH 202; one of HLH 214, HLH 215 (health/nutrition). Prerequisite chains per catalog: NUR 122/NUR 125/NUR 126 require NUR 50; NUR 131 requires NUR 121; NUR 132 requires NUR 122; NUR 135 requires NUR 125; NUR 136 requires NUR 126; NUR 52C requires NUR 52T; NUR 52D requires NUR 52C. The generic AS Registered Nurse program is NOT collected: the catalog publishes only an unsplit required-course list with no official term sequence (honest negative).",
